"""Blocker sentinels for the Modern SSpec live-capture lanes.

Each `it` below asserts that a KNOWN BLOCKER IS STILL IN EFFECT. That inversion
is deliberate: while a lane is blocked these are green and cost nothing, and the
moment the environment changes so the blocker clears, the sentinel turns RED and
names the follow-up work. A permanently-red placeholder would be ignored; a
sentinel that flips is a real notification.

Every probe here is a genuine runtime observation (a real call / a real process),
never a static read of source text — a file-existence or source-substring check
would prove only what somebody typed, not what the system currently does.

#
# ## Purpose and audience
# Audience: release/test-infrastructure owners. Purpose: keep a live, 
# flipping notification on every known Modern SSpec live-capture blocker
# so the moment an environment blocker clears, a red sentinel names the
# follow-up work instead of silence.
#
"""

use std.spec.*
use std.nogc_sync_mut.sffi.system.{process_run}

# The real libtorch capability probe. Declared here rather than imported so this
# sentinel does not drag the whole torch module graph into the spec.
extern fn rt_torch_available() -> bool

describe "Modern SSpec live-capture blocker sentinels":

    # TODO: [sspec-live-capture][P2] ML live-capture (T2g) blocked: libtorch unavailable, rt_torch_available() returns false. When it returns true, write live_ml_capture_spec.spl per live_audio_capture_spec.spl [blocked:libtorch-unavailable]
    it "still reports ML live capture blocked, because libtorch is unavailable in this environment":
        """MEASURED 2026-08-09, correcting an earlier claim: `rt_torch_available`
        DOES resolve under both `bin/simple run` and `bin/simple test` — the
        earlier "unknown extern function" reason was copied from a stale
        placeholder string in `test/01_unit/lib/torch_spec.spl` and was never
        re-probed. The real blocker is that libtorch itself is absent, so the
        extern answers `false`. A live ML capture needs a real forward pass,
        which cannot happen while this is false."""
        step("Call the real libtorch capability extern")
        val torch_ready = rt_torch_available()

        step("While this is false, T2g stays blocked; when it flips true this goes RED")
        expect(torch_ready).to_equal(false)

    # TODO: [sspec-verification][P1] T1 gate open: all Modern SSpec evidence verified on the Rust bootstrap seed. When a self-hosted binary is deployed, re-run the evidence specs + docgen gate on it [blocked:no-self-hosted-deploy]
    it "still reports Modern SSpec evidence as seed-verified, because the deployed binary is the bootstrap seed":
        """Every green result in this feature so far came from the disclosed Rust
        bootstrap seed, which repo policy does not accept as the normal tool. This
        sentinel watches the deployed binary itself: when a real self-hosted build
        is deployed the seed banner disappears, this turns RED, and T1's
        re-verification gate becomes both possible and required."""
        step("Ask the deployed binary to identify itself")
        val (stdout, stderr, code) = process_run("bin/simple", ["--version"])
        expect(code).to_equal(0)

        step("The seed self-discloses; while that banner is present T1 stays open")
        val identity = stdout + stderr
        expect(identity).to_contain("bootstrap seed only")
